Thank you for checking out Hemovia. This project represents personal work
and dedication, so please follow these simple and clear guidelines:

1. Permission to Use
You are welcome to view and learn from the code in this repository.
However, if you want to use, run, deploy, or host this project (whether
for personal, educational, or commercial purposes), you must get written
permission from me first. Please do not use it without asking beforehand.

2. Credit and Attribution
If I give you permission to use this project, you must give proper credit.
My full name (Siratim Mustakim Chowdhury) and the original repository link
(https://github.com/SiratimMChy/Hemovia-Frontend) must remain clearly visible
in the user interface, footer, and documentation so everyone knows where
the project came from.

3. No Modifications
If you are permitted to use this project, please use it as-is in its
original, unaltered form. Changing the code, altering the design, rebranding
it, or creating derivative versions is not allowed.

4. Using Parts of the Code in Other Projects
If you wish to take a specific part, module, or component from this project
to use in another project, you must reach out to me and get my approval
before doing so. You cannot copy or extract any code into your own project
without prior permission.

5. Non-Commercial
This project cannot be sold, monetized, or used for commercial gain. All
rights and ownership of this codebase remain exclusively with me.

If you have questions or want to request permission, feel free to message me on LinkedIn:
https://www.linkedin.com/in/siratim-mustakim-chowdhury/
